#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096449 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8b30414-400e-5c93-98d4-82299b4eb570" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Linear Combination of Two Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "2ff4e8a9-d5ef-5e00-bba9-b51e18bf1f24" :question/math-academy-id "e-4284" :question/problem "Given the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ shown below, draw the linear combination $2\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n![](images/32/325e4a450d89ee1f5db4afd237dbc7d58efafec72d080386788f0491cc35950b.png)" :question/worked-solution "- The vector $2\\mathbf{a}$ has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$ but twice the magnitude.\n- Likewise, the vector $3\\mathbf{b}$ has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$ but three times the magnitude.\n\n![](images/06/066784522a39671fe57b157c6c692f5c56295126b8ec6f150d917e783ab63400.png)\n\nNow, we can draw $3\\mathbf{b}$ starting from the head of $2\\mathbf{a}$. The resultant\n$2\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$\ngoes from the tail of $2\\mathbf{a}$ to the head of $3\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n![](images/d1/d1dd084ad4f8f717afac515471bcba679fbe545f266435a57fb1c94d0d5c9cca.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096450 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096651 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2121109d-7b73-5609-a9df-1eeed257ab1b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Statement With Linear Combinations Whose Coefficients Are Linear Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "f8325830-9c74-5bf2-866c-1c31acdcc37c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4285" :question/problem "Suppose we are given two vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ where $\\mathbf{a} \\nparallel \\mathbf{b}$. Find $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$, if\n\n$\\mathbf{a}+7\\mathbf{b}=(2\\alpha+\\beta)\\mathbf{a}-\\beta\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Since $\\mathbf{a} \\nparallel \\mathbf{b}$, the linear combination can only be written in one way. So, the coefficients of $\\mathbf{a}$ must be equal, and the coefficients of $\\mathbf{b}$ must be equal.\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get:\n\n$$\n{1 = 2α + β; 7 = - β\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nβ &= -7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting back into the first equation, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 &= 2α + β \\\\\n1 &= 2α + (-7) \\\\\n8 &= 2α \\\\\nα &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $\\alpha = 4$ and $\\beta = -7$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096970 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096651 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2121109d-7b73-5609-a9df-1eeed257ab1b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Statement With Linear Combinations Whose Coefficients Are Linear Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "815379c2-1a2e-502f-88e9-fc031e15b9ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$s = 3$ and $t =-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093795} {:answer/id #uuid "a1f896da-f25a-53e4-ac3c-bf271b59ffd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$s = 3$ and $t =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093796} {:answer/id #uuid "c5a93eff-2597-5f20-9e9a-88546a01c848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$s = 3$ and $t = 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093797} {:answer/id #uuid "48a4eb85-e4e4-5fca-9c6d-be8aa3f29fe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$s =-3$ and $t =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093798} {:answer/id #uuid "7346fe82-3d08-5a9e-a3ad-7377097cd7b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$s = 2$ and $t =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093799}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d0aa4fe7-2cc8-577f-85fb-d7c9d634e92d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093794}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e29e9257-b1b8-5da4-a181-19b32ffa49a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-11381" :question/problem "Suppose we are given two vectors $a$ and $b$ where $a∦b$. Find $s$ and $t$, if\n$5a + 4b = (2s + t)a + (s - t)b$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8b30414-400e-5c93-98d4-82299b4eb570" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Linear Combination of Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d1a9505-4a57-58e9-980d-c757aef01b68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9d/9d2c12b802901e16ab38b37773ead31e68aa6b86b8186fa351af2af21e4d84e4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572390} {:answer/id #uuid "41b2c190-c96a-5b7a-8e39-3ab87babffe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0e/0e546fdbe00f491e20354feb8dd46bf27112c464a873c3a388247a2d7dcc9de9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572393} {:answer/id #uuid "b36a8732-0d62-56f7-b9eb-963fdbcde877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/de/de03a1be920089723cdf3ab761a7ab02a3bbfe085ac9eb927a7dcd7163b458b1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572515} {:answer/id #uuid "e7600fa9-42ca-564f-81ec-880c6e921c12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/95/950ecbf1899a038c92fe4e0b6a299de42ca1d3e897ce85b28cc94166e7e51665.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572568} {:answer/id #uuid "eee8e964-460c-5f6f-8867-7d295205b3b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cc/cca6562873f89aa7f36b13fe7e8c5646cbdbde98c8238abc99eda6d8b24ce1e9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572576}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b36a8732-0d62-56f7-b9eb-963fdbcde877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/de/de03a1be920089723cdf3ab761a7ab02a3bbfe085ac9eb927a7dcd7163b458b1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572515} :answer-field/id #uuid "dac0f540-8539-5e56-8a7f-2c1905324354" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572654}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "22749eae-3c2e-573a-a168-cb568838d8f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-119896" :question/problem "![](images/21/212a339585b98f156d68f2e4260c0acbb474c51782b6d72acf0b89fd5c1fe69e.png)\n\nGiven the vectors $a$ and $b$ shown above, which of the following could be the linear combination $2a-2b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that\n\n$$\n2a-2b=2a+(-2b).\n$$\n\n- The vector $2a$ has the same direction as $a$ but twice the magnitude.\n\n- The vector $-2b$ has the direction that is opposite to $b$ but twice the magnitude.\n\n![](images/c1/c1cc845ddfe16f12169625e5f8404d3d92558b885ffde8c3ab02cdb2c096f699.png)\n\nNow, we can draw $-2b$ starting from the head of $2a.$ The resultant \n\n$$\n2a-2b\n$$\n\ngoes from the tail of $2a$ to the head of $-2b.$\n\n![](images/5d/5d22db7e37ff1c5b55f1ec595da919f987a6c1fea4247cf5a075f27c198ba545.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096651 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2121109d-7b73-5609-a9df-1eeed257ab1b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Statement With Linear Combinations Whose Coefficients Are Linear Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c02f9d2-6489-5d8d-80e2-8043d16c70c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c02f9d2-6489-5d8d-80e2-8043d16c70c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572349} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab223a15-b693-5906-bf6e-72560257b340" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572635} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "915b5a1a-8b66-53b2-a236-d722c0a8dc34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "915b5a1a-8b66-53b2-a236-d722c0a8dc34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572471} :answer-field/id #uuid "c60f15ed-8ce7-5564-85f4-7485ed35b513" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2a5cac6-33f2-5ce9-8655-67db2ef94b7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-277079" :question/problem "Suppose we are given two vectors $a$ and $b$ where $a∦b.$ Find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu ,$ if \n\n$$\na-2b=(3\\lambda -\\mu )a-(\\lambda -4\\mu )b.\n$$\n\n$\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. So, the coefficients of $a$ must be equal, and the coefficients of $b$ must be equal.\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3\\lambda -\\mu &=1 \\\\ \\lambda -4\\mu &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\mu =3\\lambda -1\n$$\n\nSubstituting back into the second equation, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda -4\\mu  & =2 \\\\ \\lambda -4(3\\lambda -1) & =2 \\\\ \\lambda -12\\lambda +4 & =2 \\\\ -11\\lambda  & =-2 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\frac{2}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =3\\lambda -1 \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{2}{11}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8b30414-400e-5c93-98d4-82299b4eb570" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Linear Combination of Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e0ff1ca-08d1-5d11-a958-2853ad1d3478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4c/4c623b59994ea799279ddb9f878a4418d8885cf789a0f0fbae3f920b76dc98d6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572329} {:answer/id #uuid "141e56de-8f45-541d-80e5-6168d1b1af22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ff/ffa6ea463246b87bdbc767111d72805015ad3b40895696b54051c31a8785e30c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572337} {:answer/id #uuid "1e013e1c-7c1c-5b98-8dc9-2b995e4ac6c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c2/c2a173ea1937ac228c9f69bcba2b0f2d04cf5ad018b64912b7ba397ff9a3c068.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572354} {:answer/id #uuid "ab0a2627-b32a-5580-9b78-033d4b2da069" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d9/d9be31d60b73be662c7dfe957e932a5fcd8c37c78cb4a75551047607e65081cd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572500} {:answer/id #uuid "dba9332c-d2ae-5f67-be78-45a6264c9e39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1e/1e1de76cd9d9a36b31aa086d5373cd5e6d11c876fd47c683058e6a6741b641b1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dba9332c-d2ae-5f67-be78-45a6264c9e39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1e/1e1de76cd9d9a36b31aa086d5373cd5e6d11c876fd47c683058e6a6741b641b1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572557} :answer-field/id #uuid "9eda16f6-069f-5f9f-8e85-00b3cc377912" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572632}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e8943fb5-5821-50a1-aa29-5b9a2bc234c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-77509" :question/problem "![](images/66/667454b0cdd06afe7b722aad8ad64423491e8e13a3eb950945af7bedcb7291c9.png)\n\nGiven the vectors $a$ and $b$ shown above, which of the following could be the linear combination $-4a-3b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that\n\n$$\n-4a-3b=-4a+(-3b).\n$$\n\n- The vector $-4a$ has the direction that is opposite to $a$ and $4$ times the magnitude.\n\n- The vector $-b$ has the direction that is opposite to $b$ and $3$ times the magnitude.\n\n![](images/fb/fb02d818d2ad88acc13802287bc02fa194afba38ec018429b867fe5f21a6206e.png)\n\nNow, we can draw $-3b$ starting from the head of $-4a.$ The resultant \n\n$$\n-4a-3b\n$$\n\ngoes from the tail of $-4a$ to the head of $-3b.$\n\n![](images/e3/e30a16feb7f1fcc75789443db72de1fda10b61762401d19ee296df11aa03b09d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572681 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096650 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8b30414-400e-5c93-98d4-82299b4eb570" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Linear Combination of Two Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "112d6e45-f7c7-5fd0-9c28-59f156bc4fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9e/9ed635e991a7b8243cc125083e5f4a3d2a8dc805dde41c3518f78556d690bd11.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572333} {:answer/id #uuid "19518956-bd5f-5186-bc80-a603a1eda7da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9a/9a455b1d56f155619470063a5d08751b3a5baf19e3ecee6086397f9ff7498649.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572343} {:answer/id #uuid "1fd898bc-282c-5bec-bd5a-748eaff375ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/im